  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Countering Commercial Poaching in Gabon&apos;s Plateau Bateke National Park through Intensified Wildlife Law Enforcement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to protect wildlife populations in Gabons Plateau Batk National Park by strengthening local wildlife law enforcement capabilities. This project is intended to conserve a pristine proportion of the unique forest-savanna mosaic of the Plateau Batk and important populations of forest elephants, western lowland gorillas, reptiles, and birds by addressing the impacts of commercial poaching. Specific activities include: (1) recruitment, training, and patrol support for a ranger anti-poaching force; (2) ranger training on methods to collect law enforcement and ecological data; (3) data analysis to help guide anti-poaching patrols; and (4) camera trap surveys to assess wildlife population changes.</narrative>
  </description>
